{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/384320-hunter-jrotc-ideas-and-feedback","id":384320,"title":"Hunter JROTC - ideas and feedback","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-28T10:25:52-08:00","id":384320,"title":"Hunter JROTC - ideas and feedback","content":"So the general idea here is to have a group of innocents PC's, that catch the eye of a hunter compact or conspiracy. The PC's are at the start of the game all wards of the state, so a hunter group should fairly easily be able to gain custody of them. This should happen after the PC's have already had a bit of experience dealing with the supernatural, including a backstory containing it (which they don't know at the start of the game but will probably figure out soon enough).<br /> <br /> Now the difficult part is figuring out what hunter training might look like. I want to walk the fine line that is a relatively sane hunter. Of course most people have compunctions about sending children into dangerous situations - though it has occurred to me that different groups might have different ideas on who counts as a child. At the same time, hunters have difficult and dangerous work, and maybe it's best to expose the kids to a little more danger before they get sent off. And of course, they've already survived some encounters, and maybe in some cases you can make things a lot less dangerous for the overall group by using the kids. And hunters aren't the safest people to be around.<br /> <br /> So that's where I could use ideas. I want juuuuuust a hint of the child soldier without going overtly into that territory, enough to frustrate and worry the players without going into something that could clearly be labelled abusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4777-warkitty","name":"WarKitty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T10:51:38-08:00","id":384341,"title":"","content":"It depends on the group, I'm afraid. Some would just hand them a gun, while others will attempt to drill all the facts they know about the Supernatural into their heads.<br /> <br /> But I'd say they'd run them through exercises, work on their education (with an emphasis on stuff that will help with the monster hunting biz), and maybe use them as mascots. There will also be <i>craptons</i> of indoctrination, but that's par for the course (and no different from being raised in a normal environment).<br /> <br /> Of course, while they probably won't be sent out as main hunters, they might be sent on &quot;errands&quot;, and there is always the risk of an attack on the safehouse. And the kids could sneak out and try some hunting on the side...<br /> <br /> Mostly, though, I'd focus on one cell as part of a larger compact or conspiracy, and would emphasis the <i>strong</i> cohesion that a cell has. Emphasize that it feels like <i>family</i> - albeit, a <i>crazy</i> family, but you can't always pick and choose, right? Have the Hunters interact with them in varied ways; maybe Sally just hates kids and thinks they shouldn't be there, while Jack over there dotes on them and Dana thinks that most of them are old enough to go out and hunt. Basically, focus more on internal conflicts and less on straight &quot;monster hunting.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a strong element of choice in Hunter; unlike the other splats, you <i>can</i> retire from being a Hunter. If you don't have that candle flame burning in your heart anymore (or never really did), they'll say goodbye and let you go... because having a Hunter who <i>really</i> doesn't want to be there is counterproductive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T15:37:42-08:00","id":384555,"title":"","content":"I'm leaning towards using Union - they sort of have a nice tier 1.5 feel to them, while still having extra resources to justify certain things. Enough to be able to provide a decent education and arrange for the kids to be able to be sent to a nice college, without having to worry too much about what their superiors want. Things like hunter-psychologists and other such figures might also be nice. Of course, the kids have supernatural backgrounds that might also make them targets themselves, so they might have to learn quickly no matter what their guardians want. I also imagine the primary guardians would be those who aren't active in street work anymore - elderly or injured hunters could very well take on the task of serving as parents, and would be the most likely to get approved and remain able to pass inspection. In this day and age it's not like you can just adopt a child and whisk them away - there's going to be social worker visits and rules on taking them to therapy and rules on who you can have in your home and all sorts of bureaucratic stuff that mean you can't just pick up the kids and move them into the safehouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4777-warkitty","name":"WarKitty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}